Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Electrical Engineering and Systems Science > Image and Video Processing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 17 Dec 2025]\nL9: # Title:BioimageAIpub: a toolbox for AI-ready bioimaging data publishing\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Stefan Dvoretskii , cite6†Anwai Archit , cite7†Constantin Pape , cite8†Josh Moore , cite9†Marco Nolden L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled BioimageAIpub: a toolbox for AI-ready bioimaging data publishing, by Stefan Dvoretskii and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite10†View PDF L16: > Abstract:Modern bioimage analysis approaches are data hungry, making it necessary for researchers to scavenge data beyond those collected within their (bio)imaging facilities. In addition to scale, bioimaging datasets must be accompanied with suitable, high-quality annotations and metadata.\nL17: Although established data repositories such as the Image Data Resource (IDR) and BioImage Archive offer rich metadata, their contents typically cannot be directly consumed by image analysis tools without substantial data wrangling. Such a tedious assembly and conversion of (meta)data can account for a dedicated amount of time investment for researchers, hindering the development of more powerful analysis tools.\nL18: Here, we introduce BioimageAIpub, a workflow that streamlines bioimaging data conversion, enabling a seamless upload to HuggingFace, a widely used platform for sharing machine learning datasets and models.\nL19: Subjects:  | Image and Video Processing (eess.IV); Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2512.15820 [eess.IV]\nL21:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2512.15820v1 [eess.IV] for this version)\nL22:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15820†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Anwai Archit [cite14†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 15:12:29 UTC (249 KB)